        "Every tie that ships with the map has a relation type, dates where the source gives them, a grade and at least one dated source. The relation types are descriptive (founded, owned, lent to, funded, board seat, partner at, member of) and none of them ranks one party above another.",
        "Two grades ship. Documented means a primary or official record backs the tie. Reported means at least one reliable secondary source backs it; any primary document listed with it is context and does not by itself show the tie. Nothing weaker ships: claims that rest on a single self-published book, or on overlap in attendance, membership or marriage alone, are left out or listed under Claims checked. The one exception is what you add or change yourself in Edit mode: it stays in your browser, starts as Unrated, and is marked \"Your edit, unsourced\" until you attach a source and a grade.",
        "The same standard applies to every family and institution. A tie is included if a source shows it, whoever is involved, and left out if no source shows it. Documented ties are stated plainly, including the ones that are uncomfortable for the party concerned.",
